WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.659
Connect each melting mechanism to its setting. First, add heat: hot

00:00:04.659 --> 00:00:08.967
magma transfers energy into cooler surrounding rock, which may begin to

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:09.359
melt.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.906
Second, reduce pressure. Mantle rising below ridges or hot spots can

00:00:14.906 --> 00:00:19.049
partially melt with little temperature change. This is decompression melting.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:24.246
Third, add water. Minerals in the descending slab release water into

00:00:24.246 --> 00:00:28.143
the mantle wedge. Water lowers the melting temperature. The whole slab

00:00:28.143 --> 00:00:29.559
does not simply melt.
